[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Eurobot System Tests

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @eurobot

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Manually executed system tests. ``STATUS`` records the current result;
the team updates it by hand after each test session and writes
``Not Executed`` on a new test case. ``REQ-4`` deliberately has no test
case, so the Traceability Matrix shows what an unverified requirement
looks like.
<<<

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-1
TITLE: Measure the starting footprint
STATUS: Passed
STATEMENT: >>>
Place the robot on the table in its starting configuration and wrap a
measuring tape around its footprint. Record the perimeter.

Expected: the perimeter is at most 1200 mm.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-1
  ROLE: VERIFIES

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-2
TITLE: Measure the height
STATUS: Not Executed
STATEMENT: >>>
Remove the beacon support. Measure from the table surface to the highest
point of the robot.

Expected: the height is at most 350 mm.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-2
  ROLE: VERIFIES

[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-3
TITLE: Emergency stop under load
STATUS: Failed
STATEMENT: >>>
Drive the robot forward at full speed and press the emergency stop
button. Observe the motors and the actuators.

Expected: all motion stops, no actuator holds power, and the robot stays
unpowered until the button is released.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-3
  ROLE: VERIFIES
